1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,744
Mara has found the name for her next business.

2
00:00:05,544 --> 00:00:09,915
But in a public auction, every offer tells her competitors something.

3
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,868
Her interest. Her budget. Her next move.

4
00:00:17,668 --> 00:00:19,862
What if her offer stayed hers?

5
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,540
Meet ShadowBid.

6
00:00:25,878 --> 00:00:30,369
A privacy-first auction marketplace, launching with domain names.

7
00:00:30,706 --> 00:00:36,077
Real owner listings. DNS control checks. Public commitment counts.

8
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:41,347
In this isolated demo, Mara seals an offer.

9
00:00:42,659 --> 00:00:48,199
Her browser hashes the amount with a random secret, bound to the auction and bidder.

10
00:00:49,512 --> 00:00:53,074
No wallet connection. No on-chain bidding fee.

11
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:58,344
The downloaded receipt is her proof. Keep it private.

12
00:01:00,144 --> 00:01:04,606
In the timed practice auction, a changed receipt is rejected.

13
00:01:06,406 --> 00:01:08,921
The saved original verifies.

14
00:01:10,721 --> 00:01:13,563
These waiting periods are edited down.

15
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:19,439
The highest eligible reveal wins.

16
00:01:19,802 --> 00:01:26,515
The final price is public. Bidder identity and losing offers stay private from other participants.

17
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:30,069
The trusted operator can see revealed bids.

18
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,092
The winner gets a private invoice.

19
00:01:34,542 --> 00:01:38,459
Our wallet verified a real public-testnet deposit.

20
00:01:38,909 --> 00:01:44,067
Invoice settlement remains unverified. Production payments stay disabled.

21
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:49,209
Domains today. Broader private markets, tomorrow.

22
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:53,099
ShadowBid. Private auctions. Public outcomes.

23
00:01:53,299 --> 00:01:55,514
Try the interactive demo.
